# Backend Module Conventions

Every NestJS domain module must include:

- `*.module.ts`
- `*.controller.ts` (thin; HTTP mapping only)
- `*.service.ts` (business rules)
- `dto/` with class-validator decorated DTOs
- Repository abstraction + Prisma adapter where persistence is required
- Unit tests colocated or under `__tests__/`

## Rules

- Business logic belongs in **Services**, not controllers or repositories.
- Controllers expose `/api/v1/...` routes only.
- Use Dependency Injection; never instantiate collaborators with `new` inside services when they are injectable.
- Ban `any`. Type Prisma results into domain types.
- Soft-delete queries must exclude `deletedAt IS NOT NULL` by default.
- Emit consistent error types (domain exceptions mapped to HTTP).
- Add rate limiting and guards (JWT/RBAC) on protected routes.
- Cover services with unit tests; cover critical module wiring with integration tests.
